Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:28:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] Follow-ups to patches 05 and 09 found by the full test
 suite

- Patch 05's lifeline (setpriv) turned a missing binary into 'exited with 127'
  (PROCESS_FAILED); children.mjs lifelineExecFailed recognises setpriv's own exec failure
  and runProcess reports PROCESS_LAUNCH, as the spawn error was before the wrapper. The
  spawn mock in tests/evaluator-audit.test.mjs unwraps the lifeline (8 tests).
- Patch 09 binds the runtime's default maxTokens into every new run's policy: trials
  carry the host's token bound in their reserved policy (its hash must match the run's),
  and the legacy-store fixture comparison in tests/store-rows.test.mjs allows that
  runtime addition, as it already allows dispatch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011geBy7JvDqKuqhDyfmzd1U
